{"body":{"text":["Reading Knowledge as text takes about a quarter of a second at the command line over the five stores, where it took 0.8 s while every word was a holon (19/49). A brief is read in one read, by `sections`, a function written in the language upon the natives: a brief and the briefs it holds as sections, each a whole entering no brief, which the brief component applies, where it read a whole for every brief, level by level (20/16). A read learns what it applies before working it out, a layer at a time from the expression it carries, each layer one question of every store, and a function it names asked whole, the function and all it holds, its input and its body however deep, in one question, so it learns in a round for each function named and never one for each use within one, the next layer read off what a whole gave while the other stores are asked of it alongside (20/34); and a kind of value is told by its type alone, a kind's name and an empty mould, so it is never searched for (20/14, 20/16). Counted in rounds one after another, finding a component for a brief takes about 6 where it took 20, the breadcrumb's `wholes` 9 where 23, `sections` of The design 13 where 18, and a brief's `whole` about 6 (20/34); what a read applies is still learned every read; in the browser, once the field is fetched, a move to a brief settles in 60 to 116 ms where it took 155 to 1,269 (20/16). The engine's whole asking each store its whole as one question was built again and measured: beside the brief's one read it came within about 10 ms of the layered whole, so it stays let go (19/73, 20/14). The engine still lets go of what a use gives beyond what its function takes, without a word, which is to be refused, since nothing is to fail silently (19/39). Still between: `language/text.ts` keeps the earlier form of expressions for its own tests alone. *The read's shape the session's, at the author's word that things be as simple as possible (20/15); built.*"]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a use naming no component gives is drawn by the component that takes it, found by `taking`, a function written in the language and agnostic, the functions or components that take what is given by a type of the field: of the components realized here, those that take all that is given, as a use giving it would be judged, and by a type of the field, some placeholder taking something given of a type it takes; so a brief draws as a brief, and a list with the direction it runs as a list. Whether a function or a component takes what is given is the native `takes`, giving what each placeholder takes or null: native because how a use's args meet an input is the evaluator's own, so the rule is written once and the chassis rebuilds nothing of the engine. \"we match against multiple arguments, not only one\" (20/27); \"if it's a two-liner of an expression that can replace over 100 lines of complicated code, naturally it's the right thing to do\" (20/27). A component over a kind of value alone, a list or a string, is never found so, since many take one shape for different ends, and is drawn only where a use names it; what nothing takes by a type is drawn by the fallback the chassis is given, Value, showing any holon as its values, so nothing is left unshown, and what holds no holon is given it at once, nothing read. One found is written into the use as its `fn` where the use's store takes the change, and found again each time where not; where several fit, a chooser lists them and the person's pick is drawn, never guessed. *Picked once and written, proposed, 18/88; finding by takes and taking, the author's at 20/27, its name at 20/33, its shape the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Natives are small pure functions in code, in families: the lazy ones, `if`, `case`, `and`, `or`; values; lists; sets, which are hashed; holons, `holon`, `whole`, `in`, `out`, `follow`, `takes`; history, `log`; and patterns; and the pairs glass ships, `parse` and `print`, `steps` and `chain`, with `each`, `group` and the way back, `back`. Beside them stand legacy natives, `type`, `store`, `named`, `children` and `since` among them, kept only while functions written in the field still call them. Everything else is written in the field upon the natives, as `sections`, which the brief component reads by, `wholes` and `roots`, and `taking`, by which the chassis finds a component (20/16, 20/22, 20/28)."]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC003","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The chassis broken away:** the chassis abstracted from the components it draws, a module of its own, the components a package standing on it, and the interface no module but a program, glue let go as it is met (20/18, 20/19). *The step the author's, 20/19: \"first off, it's definitely breaking away the chassis\"; its shape the session's (20/18), agreed; built, the glue met on the way let go, the rest of the components' glue to be read next.*"]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC004","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). *Open.*"]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC005","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M84EFZ37HWC006","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
